    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "title": "Buses by violation rate",
      "type": "table",
      "description": "",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "postgres",
        "uid": "gridsense-timescaledb"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 12,
        "w": 16,
        "h": 9
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {},
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "postgres",
            "uid": "gridsense-timescaledb"
          },
          "format": "table",
          "rawQuery": true,
          "editorMode": "code",
          "rawSql": "SELECT bus_id, round(min(min_voltage_pu)::numeric, 4) AS min_voltage_pu, round(max(max_voltage_pu)::numeric, 4) AS max_voltage_pu, sum(n_violations) AS violations, round(100.0 * sum(n_violations) / nullif(sum(n_readings), 0), 2) AS violation_rate_pct FROM public_gold.mart_voltage_quality_hourly WHERE network = '$network' AND is_in_scope GROUP BY bus_id ORDER BY violation_rate_pct DESC NULLS LAST LIMIT 20"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "title": "How to read",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 16,
        "y": 12,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 9
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Only **in-scope** buses (LV load buses) are judged; slack, generator and MV buses are excluded, exactly as in the hosting-capacity code (seed `network_voltage_scope`). The band comes from the network's default framework (seed `network_voltage_limits`). Meshed transmission test cases show high rates on buses without local voltage support: a property of the network, not a pipeline error."
      }
    }
